1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,057
You gulp your water

2
00:00:01,057 --> 00:00:02,217
under a blue sky

3
00:00:02,217 --> 00:00:02,870
that should be

4
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:03,800
black.

5
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:04,614
It's only blue

6
00:00:04,614 --> 00:00:05,497
because sunlight

7
00:00:05,497 --> 00:00:06,372
keeps crashing

8
00:00:06,372 --> 00:00:07,533
into the air.

9
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,205
Sunlight is every colour

10
00:00:09,205 --> 00:00:10,330
at once.

11
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:11,440
Red rolls in

12
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,681
on long, lazy waves...

13
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:14,976
and slips right past

14
00:00:14,976 --> 00:00:15,800
the air.

15
00:00:15,839 --> 00:00:16,517
Blue comes in

16
00:00:16,517 --> 00:00:18,290
short, twitchy waves.

17
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,186
It smacks into

18
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:20,439
air molecules...

19
00:00:20,439 --> 00:00:21,198
and bounces

20
00:00:21,198 --> 00:00:22,333
everywhere.

21
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,549
So blue hits your eyes

22
00:00:23,549 --> 00:00:24,929
from every direction.

23
00:00:24,929 --> 00:00:26,333
That's your sky.

24
00:00:26,365 --> 00:00:28,170
No air, no blue:

25
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:28,913
on the Moon,

26
00:00:28,913 --> 00:00:30,276
the sky is black

27
00:00:30,276 --> 00:00:31,500
at noon.

28
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,381
At sunset,

29
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:33,342
the light crosses

30
00:00:33,342 --> 00:00:34,792
nearly forty times

31
00:00:34,792 --> 00:00:35,618
more air.

32
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:36,318
The blue's all

33
00:00:36,318 --> 00:00:37,300
bounced away...

34
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:37,790
and you get

35
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:39,367
the leftovers.

36
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:40,530
On Mars?

37
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:41,500
Backwards.

38
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,070
Butterscotch sky...

39
00:00:43,070 --> 00:00:44,290
blue sunset.

40
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:45,367
Blame the dust.

41
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:47,660
You can swallow now.

